d credit. In 2028 a $2,000,000 QDOT principal distribution (event 1) is made, the first-round tax paid from the trust: compute the first-round tax and the incremental second-round tax.","scope":"Two predeceased spouses (the only supported chain length). D1 died 2025 (portability elected; examination set the base at $8.2M); D2, remarried, died 2026 holding D1 DSUE (portability elected). The survivor S died 2026: $31M gross, $1M §2053 deductions, $2M 2020 taxable gifts. A $2M QDOT principal distribution (event 1) followed in 2028. Death-date order is validated in the test suite, not in this case. The second QDOT round is computed; rounds 3+ are flagged truncation. Each decedent figure uses the death-year basic exclusion as a cited case fact ($13.99M for 2025, $15M for 2026); the §2001(c) top-bracket row (bracket-12) is a case fact read from the pinned sidecar. No §2013/2014/2012(d) credits, marital deduction, or spouse-estate counterfactual beyond the asserted history link.","steps":[{"label":"dsue_gen1_final","request":{"args":["urn:irc:example:estate-d1","?amount"],"deadlinePolicy":"urn:us:irc:core#IRC_CALENDAR_STEP","kind":"collect","legalTime":"2025-06-30","package":"us-irc-estate-gift","predicate":"urn:us:irc:estate_gift:clir#dsue_gen1_final"}},{"label":"dsue_gen2_final","request":{"args":["urn:irc:example:estate-d2","?amount"],"deadlinePolicy":"urn:us:irc:core#IRC_CALENDAR_STEP","kind":"collect","legalTime":"2026-06-30","package":"us-irc-estate-gift","predicate":"urn:us:irc:estate_gift:clir#dsue_gen2_final"}},{"label":"applicable_exclusion_amount","request":{"args":["urn:irc:example:estate-s","?amount"],"deadlinePolicy":"urn:us:irc:core#IRC_CALENDAR_STEP","kind":"collect","legalTime":"2026-06-30","package":"us-irc-estate-gift","predicate":"urn:us:irc:estate_gift:clir#applicable_exclusion_amount"}},{"label":"estate_tax","request":{"args":["urn:irc:example:estate-s","?amount"],"deadlinePolicy":"urn:us:irc:core#IRC_CALENDAR_STEP","kind":"collect","legalTime":"2026-